    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2ee8cfa1-e1ec-5551-b2e6-3d95b3980638" activityNameId="0f0e6b2f-d623-53e7-9086-75b8ff836159" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, geopolymer concrete pipe, DN 300, profile 2</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, geopolymer concrete pipe, DN 300, profile 2
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: b668a948-5837-4814-bf29-93b11fabbecc
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with geopolymer concrete pipe. DN 300, profile 2 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with geopolymer concrete pipe, DN 300, profile 1. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 300, profile 1 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Geopolymer concrete pipe, 300 mm, outer diameter 440 mm, wall thickness 70 mm, 187 kg/m, 2300 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b668a948-5837-4814-bf29-93b11fabbecc.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
